Fused dense corundum is a new type of high-purity refractory materials formed by using high-purity alumina and reducing agent in a certain ratio, smelting in electric arc furnace and cooled. The main crystal phase is α-Al2O3 and color is light gray.
White fused alumina is a high-grade abrasive raw material, made of high-quality industrial alumina powder after being melted at a high temperature above 2200℃ in an electric tilting furnace and then cooled. Its main crystal phase is α-Al2O3, and the color is white.
After sandblasting, the surface is white and without any impurities,no need complex cleaning;
Fused Alumina Magnesia Spinel is a new type of high-purity synthetic refractory material made from alumina and high-purity light-burned magnesia as the main raw materials in an electric tilting furnace after being melted at a high temperature of more than 2000 ℃ and then cooled. Features
