Solar frame aluminum profiles may encounter some defects and defects in the production process. Today we will understand the production defects of solar frame aluminum profiles and find out the reasons for these defects.
The cracks on the surface of aluminum profile extrusion are due to the excessively high temperature of the ingot blank and the excessively fast extrusion speed. It may also be a mold problem, the film hole is not lubricated enough, the guide path is not installed or the guide path is not suitabl
Bending and twisting are mainly due to improper membrane hole design, improper lubrication, excessive extrusion speed or improper guide path.
This is mainly the problem of the squeeze cylinder. The gap between the squeeze cylinder and the squeeze pad is too large, the inner wall of the squeeze cylinder is worn out, and the squeeze cylinder/squeeze pad is stuck with oil and water; aluminum rods are oil stains on the surface, trachoma and pores on the surface, the temperature of the extrusion cylinder and the aluminum rod are too high; the extrusion die has oil stains, etc.
