The formation of aluminum rods is about three steps, batching, smelting, and casting. According to production needs, calculate and match different alloy components and various raw materials; then put the matched materials into the furnace to melt; finally, the refined aluminum liquid is forged into different shapes of aluminum rods.
Depending on the elements contained in the aluminum rod, there are also different applications for the aluminum rod:
2000 series: This series has the highest copper content and the highest hardness. It belongs to aviation aluminum, which is not common in general industry and is used for aircraft components, screw components, rivets, etc.
4000 series: This series has high silicon content, so its wear resistance is good, and it is often used as machine parts, forging materials, etc., with low melting point, and is used as welding material. 5000 series: The main element of this series is magnesium, which is the most commonly used aluminum rod material in life.
6000 series: This series contains two elements, magnesium and silicon. It is a combination of the characteristics of 4000 series and 5000 series.
8000 Series: Most applications are aluminum foil.
