One of the most frequent doubts that we usually have when we live with a furry one is that of why can't cats eat chocolate. If you want to know, keep reading because today we are going to unravel the mystery.
1 What is theobromide and why can't my cat eat chocolate?
What is theobromide and why can't my cat eat chocolate?
Chocolate contains caffeine, theobromine and a high fat content. The most toxic forms for cats are cocoa powder and chocolate bars for cooking.
La theobromine is the major toxic component of chocolate and main cause of poisoning due to ingestion of chocolate in cats and dogs.
Being milk chocolate is that it has less toxicity. Therefore, if your kitten ate even a small piece of this food, his life could be in danger.
The symptoms are very varied, these being the following:
Increase in blood pressure.
In very serious cases, that is, in those in which the intake has been very high, the animal could die in just 24 hours. So if your cat has eaten chocolate, It is very important that you take him to a veterinary center as soon as possible to avoid reaching that situation.
Do not try to make him vomit at home, since with cats it is quite complicated and we could cause more damage.
If you do not have activated charcoal at home, it may be good to give it water or food to reduce absorption in the stomach and thus reduce symptoms.
If it is absolutely certain that what you have eaten is chocolate, the first thing they will do at the veterinary center is to induce vomiting and perform a gastric lavage. And then you will be given activated charcoal mixed with water through a syringe.
Also, in the event that your cat needs to be hospitalized for more days and has pancreatititis, a jejunostomy tube can even be placed. With this probe it is achieved that the pancreas does not work during the recovery period.
