Tryout When receiving a new mold for proofing and testing, I always eager to try a result earlier and hope the process goes smoothly so as not to waste man-hours and cause trouble.
It is best to obtain the design drawing of the mold, analyze it in detail, and ask a mold technician to participate in the trial work.
Pay attention to whether there are scratches, missing parts, looseness, etc., whether the movement of the mold toward the slide plate is correct, whether there is any leakage in the water channel and air pipe joints, and if there are restrictions on the mold opening, it should also be marked on the mold. If the above actions can be done before hanging the mold, it is possible to avoid the waste of man-hours when the problem is found when hanging the mold and then the mold is disassembled.
(c) Maximum departure
After everything is confirmed that there is no problem, the next step is to hang the mold. When hanging, be careful not to remove all the clamping templates and before opening the mold, so as to prevent the clamping template from loosening or breaking and causing the mold to fall.
After the mold temperature is increased, the movement of each part must be checked again, because the steel may cause a jam phenomenon after thermal expansion, so pay attention to the sliding of each part to avoid strain and vibration.
Do not try the mold completely with the inferior material. If there is a color requirement, you can arrange the color test together.
In order to prevent the finished product from short shot, fracture, deformation, burrs and even damage to the mold.
If the processing cycle is too long, the weak parts of the mold core may be broken due to the shrinkage of the rubber material. Of course, you can’t predict all the problems that may occur in the trial mold process, but full consideration and timely measures can help you avoid serious and expensive losses.
In order to avoid unnecessary waste of time and troubles during mass production, it is indeed necessary to pay patience to adjust and control various processing conditions, find the best temperature and pressure conditions, and formulate standard test procedures, which can be used in Establish daily working methods.
2) The material pipe must be cleaned thoroughly to prevent the inferior glue or miscellaneous materials from being injected into the mold, because the inferior glue and miscellaneous materials may jam the mold. Test whether the temperature of the barrel and the temperature of the mold are suitable for the raw materials to be processed.
4) Wait patiently until the conditions of the machine and mold stabilize, even for medium-sized machines, it may take more than 30 minutes. You can use this time to view possible problems with the finished product.
8) Measure and record the important dimensions of continuous samples (we should wait for the samples to cool to room temperature before measuring).
2) Adjust the machine conditions according to the size of all finished products that are too large or too small. If the shrinkage rate is too large and the finished product appears to be insufficient to shoot, you can also increase the gate size by referring to it.
After reviewing all the recorded values, keep a set of samples for proofreading to compare whether the corrected samples have improved.
